course: dictionary
lesson: 5823
title: A title of respect
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mahatma is a title. It means «great soul», and in India it is given to a person who is very wise, good and respected.
explain: With a capital letter, Mahatma usually means one man: Mahatma Gandhi. «Mahatma» is a title of respect, not his first name. His first name was Mohandas.
explain: Use the context to check. «India won independence from Britain in 1947 after decades of peaceful campaigning led by figures such as Mahatma Gandhi.» Peaceful campaigning and leaders show that Mahatma is a name of honour.
fact: A mahatma is a title meaning «great soul».
fact: In India, the title is given to a person who is very wise, good and respected.
fact: «Mahatma Gandhi» (1869–1948) led Indians in non-violent protest against British rule.
fact: In 1930, his Salt March protested against a British tax on salt.
fact: «Mahatma» is a title, not his first name: Gandhi's first name was Mohandas.
exercise: «India won independence from Britain in 1947 after decades of peaceful campaigning led by figures such as Mahatma Gandhi.» What does Mahatma mean here? | A type of British tax | A kind of salt | The name of a river in India | *A title of respect meaning great soul
exercise: What did Gandhi's Salt March of 1930 protest against? | *A British tax on salt | The rising price of bread | A new school for children | A war with another country
exercise: Mahatma Gandhi led people in protest. What kind of protest was it? | Violent and fast | *Non-violent and peaceful | Secret and hidden | Loud and angry
test: In India, who is called a mahatma? | A very rich trader | A king's soldier | A teacher of maths | *A very wise, good and respected person
test: Is «Mahatma» Gandhi's first name? | *No, it is a title of respect, and his first name was Mohandas | Yes, it was his first name | No, it is a British tax | Yes, it was his surname
exam: What is true about «Mahatma»? | *It is a title of respect meaning great soul | It is a British tax on salt | It is his first name | It means salt
